      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T15:00:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Collection fetch duplicates the helper that already handles $expand.\n\nfetchTasks always GETs /redfish/v1/TaskService/Tasks, then GETs every member. bmcweb’s collection entries are { \"@odata.id\" } only, and maxTaskCount is 100, so an active list is up to 101 conditional GETs every 5 seconds. The ETag client (ttl: 0) revalidates each one; it does not serve a stale body, so progress can update, but the fan-out is real.\n\n`useRedfishCollection` already checks ProtocolFeaturesSupported.ExpandQuery and falls back when $expand fails.\n\n`useSensors` is the pattern to follow. Skipping $expand up front because some BMCs return 501 is already handled there. useTaskService() is never called. The composable imports @/store/api; new composables in this tree are supposed to import @/api/client (src/store/api.js is a Vuex re-export of that client).\n\nThe “already expanded” check (TaskState or Name on every member) is looser than membersAreExpanded() in useRedfishCollection, which treats any non-@odata property as expanded. A partial member would skip the detail GET and lose Payload and PercentComplete.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "d7c2e36cdbc9a7136312b086b4c6201a5abc6dfc",
