      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T15:00:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The poll covers the table with the loading bar.\n\n`isBusy` is isLoading || isFetching || isCancelling, and a watcher calls startLoader() / endLoader() whenever isBusy changes. refetchInterval sets isFetching every 5 seconds while any task is active, and again on window focus.\n\nendLoader() holds the global bar up for a full second.\n\nWhile a task is running, the page this change adds strobes the top progress bar and marks the table busy, which is when the percent column needs to stay readable. isBusy should be the initial load and the cancel request. Background refetches should update the rows in place. placeholderData already keeps the previous rows; isFetching throws that away by forcing the busy state.",
