      "message": "Removing cancel is right. Both task routes in bmcweb register GET only.\n\nThe adapted success rule is right too. percentComplete starts at 0 and dump tasks leave it there, so requiring 100 would mark those Completed/OK tasks as failed. Firmware update does advance PercentComplete, including to 100, and that still counts as success. A Completed/OK task that stopped between 0 and 100 stays unsuccessful.\n\nA Pinia store can wait for the SSE work. This page is one Vue Query cache with no other client state.",
